  "title": "India's Semiconductor Push Expands into Everyday Products and Infrastructure",
  "summary": "India is expanding its semiconductor presence by targeting everyday products such as cars, TVs, and power infrastructure, alongside building capabilities across design, fabrication, and equipment. The government has committed Rs 1.27 lakh crore for the second phase of the semiconductor programme to enhance domestic and global capabilities.",
